      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793706725541,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "text": "Artifact storage\n    The Kubernetes Pods store two kinds of data:\n        Metadata\n            Experiments, jobs, runs, single scalar metrics\n             (generally aggregated for the purposes of sorting\n              and filtering), etc. Kubeflow Pipelines \n            stores the metadata in a MySQL database.\n        \n        Artifacts\n            Pipeline packages, views, large-scale metrics like\n             time series (usually used for investigating an\n             individual run’s performance and for debugging), \n            etc. Kubeflow Pipelines stores the artifacts in\n             an artifact store like MinIO server, Google Cloud Storage (GCS), or Amazon S3.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Artifact storage\n    The Kubernetes Pods store two kinds of data:\n        Metadata\n            Experiments, jobs, runs, single scalar metrics\n             (generally aggregated for the purposes of sorting\n              and filtering), etc. Kubeflow Pipelines \n            stores the metadata in a MySQL database.\n        \n        Artifacts\n            Pipeline packages, views, large-scale metrics like\n             time series (usually used for investigating an\n             individual run’s performance and for debugging), \n            etc. Kubeflow Pipelines stores the artifacts in\n             an artifact store like MinIO server, Google Cloud Storage (GCS), or Amazon S3.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": 1793611124232,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
